{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"princely-courageous-milksnake","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Symptom\n\nThe hourly LaunchAgent `com.navapbc.rebar-dev-update`, which keeps this host's **global**\n`rebar` / `rebar-mcp` aligned to `origin/main`, has failed **119 consecutive times**. The global\nbuild is pinned at `cdfd7d94dc2fe7671a7eba48e31f36c30f39235c` (2026-08-28) — roughly **195 commits\nbehind** `origin/main` and about five days stale. `launchctl list` reports last exit status **1**\nfor the agent (the sibling `rebar-worktree-gc` and `rebar-serena-mirror-update` agents report 0).\n\nEvery hourly run logs the same rejection:\n\n```\n2026-09-03T23:29:51Z start (installed-good=cdfd7d94d... remote-main=ebbcd7a030d6...)\nerror: Required uv version `==0.12.7` does not match the running version `0.12.6`\n2026-09-03T23:32:05Z candidate ebbcd7a030d6... rejected at sync; current left untouched\n2026-09-03T23:32:06Z candidate-rejection streak now 119 (latest stage: sync)\n```\n\n118 of the 119 rejections are this uv mismatch; one is an unrelated transient\n(`fetch-pack: unexpected disconnect ... early EOF`, rejected at the `checkout` stage).\n\n## Root cause: an inverted assumption, not a missing upgrade\n\n`~/.local/bin/rebar-dev-update.sh:18` hardcodes the uv binary:\n\n```sh\nUV_BIN=\"${REBAR_DEV_UV_BIN:-/opt/homebrew/bin/uv}\"\n```\n\nand `:120` deliberately orders PATH to keep that binary authoritative, with the reasoning stated\nat `:116-118`:\n\n```sh\n# launchd gives a minimal PATH. Keep Homebrew before ~/.local/bin so the obsolete\n# standalone uv there cannot shadow the pinned UV_BIN.\nexport PATH=\"/opt/homebrew/bin:${HOME}/.local/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin\"\n```\n\nMeasured on this host:\n\n| binary | version | date |\n|---|---|---|\n| `/opt/homebrew/bin/uv` | **0.12.6** | Homebrew, 2026-08-25 |\n| `/Users/joeoakhart/.local/bin/uv` | **0.12.7** | standalone, 2026-08-27 |\n\nThe repo pins `required-version = \"==0.12.7\"` in `pyproject.toml:346` (landed in commit\n`7501cc1d602d`, \"Pin uv once so CI stops resolving it remotely\"). uv reads `required-version`\nitself and fails fast, so `:344`'s `\"$UV_BIN\" sync` aborts every run.\n\n**The comment's premise has inverted.** When it was written the `~/.local/bin` standalone was the\nobsolete one, so pinning to Homebrew was right. Homebrew is now the stale side. The guard written\nto prevent a stale uv from being selected is now the mechanism selecting a stale uv. Hardcoding\neither absolute path just re-inverts the next time one side updates first.\n\n## This is the same pin that caused a production outage\n\n`required-version = \"==0.12.7\"` also broke the on-box container builds when their Dockerfiles used\na floating `uv:latest` tag — the root cause of the multi-hour MCP outage tracked under bug `febd`.\nThat fix pinned `infra/compose/Dockerfile.{mcp,reviewbot,opcert}` to `uv:0.12.7` and extended\n`scripts/check_uv_pin.py` to scan Dockerfiles. **This host's updater is a third consumer of the same\npin that was never brought along**, and it is outside `check_uv_pin.py`'s reach because it is a\nmachine-local script, not a tracked repo file.\n\n## The alert built to catch exactly this cannot deliver\n\n`docs/local-env-main-tracking.local.md` documents a `REJECT_STREAK_ALERT` (default **3**) added\nafter a prior incident it describes as: *\"the b477339a99 incident: 43 hourly `sync` rejections,\n~48 commits behind, no signal\"*. The alert is firing correctly and failing to deliver on every\nattempt:\n\n```\naws: [ERROR]: An error occurred (AuthorizationError) when calling the Publish operation:\nUser: arn:aws:iam::820258254566:user/joeoakhart is not authorized to perform: SNS:Publish\non resource: arn:aws:sns:us-east-1:896586841071:rebar-gerrit-alerts\nbecause no resource-based policy allows the SNS:Publish action\nERROR: aws sns publish failed for alert 'reject-streak'\n```\n\nThe IAM principal is in account **820258254566**; the SNS topic is in account **896586841071**.\nNo resource-based policy on the topic permits the cross-account publish. So the streak reached\n**119 against a threshold of 3** with zero operator signal — a strictly worse recurrence of the\nvery incident the alert was introduced to prevent. **The detection gap is the more important half\nof this bug: without it, the next stall is equally silent regardless of what caused it.**\n\n## Impact\n\nEvery agent session on this host that invokes the global `rebar` has, for about five days, been\nrunning a build ~195 commits stale. The gate's own advisory says it plainly:\n\n> \"this rebar build (cdfd7d94d, 2026-08-29, dirty) is 195 commit(s) BEHIND the ref this gate\n> pinned (08a39c39c) — it may predate recent config keys and gate fixes, so **results can be wrong\n> in ways the verdict cannot show**.\"\n\nThat reaches plan-review and completion-verifier verdicts produced through the global tool, not\njust this session's. This was noticed only because a subagent's gate log was read closely.\n\n## Secondary defect observed\n\n`~/.local/state/rebar-dev/launchd.err.log` shows the pruner failing to reclaim release dirs:\n\n```\nrm: .../releases/5b5008bbfbec...66068/.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages: Directory not empty\nrm: .../releases/5fb693345b0c...1559: Directory not empty\n```\n\n`releases/5fb693345b0cd1b48d1e9d20b292fd15761c7624.1559` is a 3-entry stub — a partially built\nrelease that was never completed or cleaned. Related to the disk-ceiling work under epic\n`6202-e1c7-c57f-4897`, since these release dirs are ~346 MB each.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\nAll deterministic and verifiable in a single run — no waiting for the hourly timer or for a\nrecurrence.\n\n1. Running the updater on demand\n   (`launchctl kickstart -k gui/$(id -u)/com.navapbc.rebar-dev-update`) publishes a `current`\n   whose `sha` equals `origin/main` at that moment, and appends no `Required uv version` error to\n   `update.log`. `reject-streak` returns to 0.\n2. The updater selects a uv that **satisfies the repo's declared `required-version`**, rather than\n   hardcoding an absolute path to either candidate. It must not be re-broken by whichever of\n   Homebrew / standalone updates first next time. If no available uv satisfies the pin, the run\n   must fail with a message naming the required version, the version found, and the paths\n   inspected — never a bare mismatch line.\n   Verify by pointing the resolver at a deliberately wrong uv and observing that message.\n3. The reject-streak alert reaches the operator. Either the cross-account SNS publish is\n   authorized, or the sink is changed to one this host's IAM principal can actually write.\n   Verified by forcing an alert (e.g. `REBAR_DEV_ALERT_CMD` or a threshold override) and observing\n   delivery — not by waiting for the next real stall.\n4. A stalled updater is detectable **locally**, without depending on the alert path at all — for\n   example a `rebar` invocation surfacing that the running build is more than N commits behind, or\n   a check script an operator can run. Rationale: this stall persisted 119 hours because the only\n   detector was a remote sink that silently 403'd.\n5. The pruner's `Directory not empty` failures are resolved, and the partial release stub\n   `5fb693345b0cd...1559` is reclaimed.\n\n## Notes for whoever takes this\n\n- `rebar-dev-update.sh` already honours a `REBAR_DEV_UV_BIN` override, so a fix can be staged\n  without editing the script if needed for an immediate unblock.\n- The script is **machine-local** and git-ignored, so a repo-side test cannot cover it directly.\n  Consider whether `scripts/check_uv_pin.py` should grow an operator-runnable mode that checks\n  local consumers of the pin, which would satisfy AC4's spirit and stay portable (no CI provider\n  dependency).","id":"ae97-a37b-9fa3-413a","parent_id":"","priority":1,"tags":["bug","ops","tooling","local-env","alerting"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Hourly rebar-dev updater stalled 119 runs on a uv version mismatch; global rebar is ~195 commits stale and the reject-streak alert cannot deliver (cross-account SNS 403)"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788481636576004001,"uuid":"f6679091-b9e8-4f3f-9e1f-eb69f21d4816"}